  "slug": "reverse-string",
  "title": "Reverse String",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "category": "Two pointers",
  "patterns": [
    "two pointers"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "a built-in reverse works, but what is it actually doing under the hood?",
    "what if you had a pointer at each end of the string and swapped the characters they point to?",
    "move both pointers toward the middle after each swap, stopping when they meet or cross",
    "this is the same two-pointer shape you'll see again in palindrome checks and array reversals"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "swapping past the middle (going one step too far and un-swapping)",
    "forgetting the loop condition for odd-length strings, where the middle character shouldn't move",
    "trying to mutate an immutable string in place instead of building/returning a new one where the language requires it"
  ],
